{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"I fixed the `audit-log-archiver` CronJob and submitted the mitigation. The submission returned 200 (\"Submission received\"). I haven't seen the validation result.\n\n- **Cause:** the CronJob's `fluent-bit-sidecar` container runs forever. Each run's pod therefore never finished, and a new pod started every minute. They would have kept piling up (`concurrencyPolicy: Allow`).\n- **Fix:** I moved the sidecar into a native sidecar (an init container with `restartPolicy: Always`). I also set `concurrencyPolicy: Forbid` and `activeDeadlineSeconds: 120`. I deleted the two stuck jobs and recreated the CronJob.\n- **Check:** the next scheduled job completed, with its pod showing `Completed`.\n- **App state:** the app's own pods were all `Running`, and a hotel-search request through the frontend returned results normally. I didn't find a fault in the application services themselves, so this CronJob was the only problem I fixed.\n\nThe native sidecar needs Kubernetes 1.29 or later; the new job ran correctly, so this cluster supports it."}}
